# CLAUDE.local.md — operator-local overlay pointer

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (which is **gitignored**) and fill in your
site details. Claude Code auto-reads `CLAUDE.local.md`; it never ships with the
repo, so it's the right place for site-specific pointers.

This repo (`proxmox-lab`) is **site-agnostic**. Everything specific to YOUR
deployment lives in a separate **overlay directory** outside the repo. See
`docs/getting-started/local-overlay.md` for the full structure.

---

**Overlay directory:** `~/<your-site>-lab/`   <!-- e.g. ~/acme-lab/ -->

That directory holds your `bootstrap.yml`, Terraform tfvars overlay,
`crypto/`, `cluster-info.json`, cross-session `memory/`, `project-updates/`,
and a site `CLAUDE.md` describing your topology, IPs, hostnames, and
credential paths.

**Before any decision that depends on site-specific values**, read
`~/<your-site>-lab/CLAUDE.md`.

**Auto-memory** for this repo lives at `~/<your-site>-lab/memory/`.

